claimed: acme-dns01 -- the last of the three, and the only road to a WILDCARD. The CA asks for a TXT record `_acme-challenge.<domain>` holding base64url(SHA-256(keyAuthorization)) instead of a file this server answers; the protocol half is small, the reason it was deferred is that writing a DNS record needs a provider and this repository has no DNS seam. So: a `Dns` trait (put/remove) beside `Challenges`, NO provider shipped, the challenge type chosen per authorization (dns-01 when a `Dns` is given, and REQUIRED for a wildcard, which http-01 cannot answer at all), and the propagation wait as a named, configurable pause rather than a hidden sleep. Tested for real: pebble-challtestsrv as both the DNS server Pebble resolves against and the provider our test `Dns` writes to over its HTTP API -- a wildcard issued end to end. Touches Acme.scala, specs/acme.md, docs.
